# IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN

# VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

# BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

# THE REGENT OF BENGKAYANG,

Considering:  
a. that in every human being there are inherent human rights that must be respected, upheld and protected by the state, law, Regional Government and every person for the sake of honor and protection of human dignity and worth;  
b. that in reality the number of children in Bengkayang Regency exceeds one third of the population, so that the Regional Government is obligated to provide protection to children from all forms of violence, discrimination and exploitation, in order to ensure a decent and dignified life and livelihood for children of Bengkayang Regency;  
c. that child issues must be handled comprehensively, in an integrated, directed and sustainable manner, thus requiring institutional support through legislation to support Bengkayang as a Child-Friendly Regency;  
d. that based on Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection and Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence, the Regional Government together with the community is obligated to undertake prevention, protection, and recovery efforts for victims of violence;  

• In View of:  
-2- ,,  
e. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c, and letter d, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence;  
